{
  "what": "Weight-loading cost on the kernel Canonical ships, four ways: vLLM as shipped (writable MAP_PRIVATE mapping), --safetensors-load-strategy eager, vllm#49991's VLLM_ROCM_CLONE_MMAP_WEIGHTS, and safetensors 0.8.0's backend=\"pread\". Measured 2026-08-23 on 7.0.0-30.30~24.04.1.",
  "why": "vllm#49991 rested on two magnitudes: a kernel regression worth whole seconds per copy, and a permanent 4-8x penalty for writable mappings. Ubuntu fixed the first in 7.0.0-30 on 2026-08-20. This is what the second one is worth end to end, which the repository had only ever estimated by arithmetic.",
  "date": "2026-08-23",
  "machine": {
    "gpu": "2x Radeon RX 7900 XT (gfx1100), TP=1, VFIO guest",
    "kernel": "7.0.0-30.30~24.04.1 (#30~24.04.1-Ubuntu SMP, built 2026-08-07)",
    "userspace": "rocm/vllm 7.14.0, PyTorch 2.11.0, vLLM 0.23.1.dev1+g9ddef7117, safetensors 0.8.0",
    "ram_gib": 23.4,
    "swap_gib": 8,
    "storage": "ext4 on /dev/sdb, 1931-2114 MiB/s cold sequential read, measured the same session"
  },
  "method": {
    "harness": "One script iterates the checkpoint through vllm's safetensors_weights_iterator and copies every tensor to device 0. Timer starts after the HIP context is warm. Each cell is a fresh process, so the process is the replication unit.",
    "page_cache": "Controlled. Every cell in the matrix, three-way and moe phases is preceded either by drop_caches (cold) or by drop_caches plus a full read of the checkpoint (warm). The 2026-07-28 run had no such control and loaded three models in sequence, so each cell inherited its predecessor's cache.",
    "resident_set": "RssAnon and RssFile are sampled every 64 tensors during the load. safetensors unmaps a shard as soon as the iterator leaves it, so an end-of-loop sample sees an empty process; the first attempt at this measured nothing and was discarded.",
    "phases": {
      "matrix": "8B and 12B x {warm,cold} x {baseline,eager,flag} x 3 reps, plus 31B cold x {baseline,flag} x 2",
      "three-way": "8B and 12B x {warm,cold} x {baseline,flag,pread} x 2 reps, plus 31B cold x 3 modes, with the resident-set split",
      "moe": "gemma-4-26B-A4B-AWQ, 23 GB in 4 shards and ~35 743 mostly small tensors, cold x 3 modes x 2 reps",
      "july-ordering-control": "the 2026-07-28 ordering replayed with no cache control, to separate method from kernel",
      "end-to-end": "a real vllm serve startup, reading the loader's own 'Loading weights took' line"
    }
  },
